  "details": "RRD::CGI::Image versions through 0.01 for Perl pass CGI query parameters containting \"tz\" to tzset(), , so a FIFO or device path blocks the CGI process.\n\nThe normalize_params method sends any query key matching /tz/i to tz(), which sets $ENV{TZ} to that value, with no validation. It then calls tzset(). glibc treats a TZ value starting with / or : as a file path and opens it, so a value naming a FIFO or a blocking device stalls the process inside tzset().",
